---
import Film from '../../plate/Film.astro';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { CUES, TIMELINE } from './story';
import './style.css';

const labels = [
  { id: 'equation', tex: String.raw`\Delta u=u^3-u` },
  { id: 'phase-limits', tex: String.raw`u\to-1\qquad u\to+1` },
  { id: 'profile', tex: String.raw`g(s)=\tanh(s/\sqrt2)` },
  { id: 'flat-wall', tex: String.raw`u(x)=\tanh((e\cdot x-c)/\sqrt2)` },
  { id: 'circle-wall', tex: String.raw`u(x)=\tanh((|x|-3)/\sqrt2)` },
  { id: 'cone-norms', tex: String.raw`\rho_1=\rho_2` },
  { id: 'end-limits', tex: String.raw`u(x^{\boldsymbol{\prime}},t)\longrightarrow\pm1\quad(t\longrightarrow\pm\infty)` },
  { id: 'monotone-domain', tex: String.raw`u\in C^2(\mathbb R^8,(-1,1))` },
  { id: 'monotone-rise', tex: String.raw`\Delta u=u^3-u,\quad\partial_8u>0` },
  { id: 'monotone-parameters', tex: String.raw`e\in\mathbb S^7,\quad e_8>0,\quad c\in\mathbb R` },
  { id: 'stable-domain', tex: String.raw`v\in C^2(\mathbb R^7,[-1,1])` },
  { id: 'stable-equation', tex: String.raw`\Delta v=v^3-v` },
  { id: 'stable-profile', tex: String.raw`v(x)=\tanh((a\cdot x-b)/\sqrt2)` },
  { id: 'stable-parameters', tex: String.raw`a\in\mathbb S^6,\quad b\in\mathbb R` },
] as const;
---

<Film
  tag="uruk-flat-walls"
  cues={CUES}
  timeline={TIMELINE}
  step={50}
  labels={labels}
  description="A stippled square shows a flat wall between two phases, with its hyperbolic tangent profile alongside it. The same window rotates through four tested directions and bends into a circular wall whose nonzero residual shows it is not a solution. It resets to a flat wall and shrinks into a dimension strip. An inset plots the two equal block norms of points on the eight-dimensional Simons cone. This is a nonlinear projection, not a literal plane slice or an Allen-Cahn solution. A historical row marks dimensions two and three as proved, four through eight as conditional before September 2026, and counterexamples from nine. Blue outlines identify only the paper's monotone claim in eight dimensions and its stable claim in seven. The ending keeps the historical strip and dated review evidence. A full text transcript follows."
  caption="A flat wall solves the Allen-Cahn equation. De Giorgi asked whether every solution rising in one direction must be flat through dimension eight. The strip first shows the frontier before September 2026. The paper claims the monotone endpoint in eight and stable rigidity in seven."
  leftOut="the proof, its four parts, energy estimates and surface tension; the human results in dimensions three and four from September 2026; other double-well potentials; dimension one. The circular field is not a solution or a counterexample. The Simons cone is not a graph or an Allen-Cahn solution."
>
  <p class="film-method">How the film is made. The browser computes the stipple from <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`u(x)=\tanh((e\cdot x-c)/\sqrt2)`, false)} />. A denser stipple means a value nearer −1. The phase values ±1 are limits of this transition, not values it attains at finite points. Its one-dimensional profile satisfies <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`g''=g^3-g`, false)} /> exactly. The shown finite-difference residuals are numerical checks of four examples with spacing 0.01. Finite sample checks do not prove the identity or the paper's theorem.</p>
  <p class="film-method">The four directions and offsets, their sample points and the six cone inputs are fixed by the direction's check script. The browser recomputes the fields, second differences and cone norms from those inputs. The circular field uses <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`u(x)=\tanh((|x|-3)/\sqrt2)`, false)} />. Its residual on the circle is <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`1/(3\sqrt2)\approx0.2357`, false)} />. It is also nonsmooth at the centre and does not satisfy the global monotonicity hypothesis. It illustrates a failed bent wall, not a counterexample to De Giorgi's conjecture. The carried window returns to a flat wall before entering the strip.</p>
  <p class="film-method">The cone inset plots <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`\rho_1=\sqrt{x_1^2+\cdots+x_4^2}`, false)} /> against <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`\rho_2=\sqrt{x_5^2+\cdots+x_8^2}`, false)} /> for points of the Simons cone in eight-dimensional space. Both norms are equal. The diagonal is a nonlinear norm projection, not a literal two-dimensional slice of the cone. The cone is area-minimizing but is not a minimal graph, and it is not an Allen-Cahn solution. The non-flat minimal-graph and monotone Allen-Cahn thresholds occur in ambient dimension nine. The stable Allen-Cahn counterexamples in dimension eight are a separate fact.</p>
  <p class="film-method">The first strip is explicitly historical, before September 2026. Its hatching in dimensions four through eight means Savin's additional end-limit assumption. Two human groups removed that assumption in dimension four during September 2026; those results are left out of this strip. A cross beside dimension nine marks failure of universal rigidity. Counterexamples exist, and flat walls still solve the equation. The small wall and non-flat icons are schematic illustrations of cited results.</p>
  <p class="film-method">The blue marks identify claims for the scalar quartic equation only. The monotone statement concerns an entire <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`C^2`, false)} /> solution on <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`\mathbb R^8`, false)} /> with values strictly between −1 and 1 and strictly positive derivative in the eighth coordinate. Its claimed conclusion has <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`e\in\mathbb S^7`, false)} />, <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`e_8>0`, false)} /> and a real shift. Energy growth, minimization and the end limits are not assumed. The stable statement concerns <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`v\in C^2(\mathbb R^7,[-1,1])`, false)} /> with nonnegative second variation. It permits the actual constants ±1 as well as a flat transition, with a unit vector in <span set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`\mathbb S^6`, false)} /> and a real shift. No energy-growth assumption is imposed. The unfilled stable cells in dimensions two through six mean not shown, not unknown.</p>
  <p class="film-method">The closing ledger follows the article's date, 20 October 2026. No mathematician had publicly reported reading or checking the proof. The pinned release has no family-375 Lean scope note or comparator statement; this does not assert that it contains no related Lean modules. No machine proof replay is performed here. The film illustrates examples and statements, not a check of the written proof. With JavaScript disabled the article and transcript remain available. Reduced motion uses one completed drawing per cue.</p>
</Film>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
